  "units": "Hessian eigenvalues of the canonical 486-real chart, units of the benchmark scale M (|Phi|=1)",
  "verdict": "The certified G3 point is a strict local minimum (modulo its 38 symmetry directions) of the benchmark potential, with global minimality open, but it is not a Standard-Model vacuum: its Delta_R is the T3R = 0, Y = -1 component of the 126bar triplet, so hypercharge breaks at r M_GUT and the unbroken group is SU(3) x SU(2)_L x U(1)_T3R; its 10_H vev also breaks SU(2)_L with |<H>|/|<Phi>| = 1. At (F, r Delta_R, H=0) every 10_H mode is tachyonic and, for this Delta_R, each five-plet is split only by beta r^2 = 1/500; retuning O06 alone to 0 leaves one massless (1,2,2) doublet. An SM-preserving G3 target needs the Y = 0 singlet of the 126bar (with p: the standard SM; with F: SU(5), so the flipped direction). Nothing is closed or excluded here."
